  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1223 PM CDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nTemperatures remain hot through the long term, however, we will see \na slight \"cooling\" trend beginning Thursday. The upper trough \nmentioned in the short term discussion will continue to expand \nacross western CONUS on Thursday. This will push the upper ridging \nfarther east with the western edge sitting directly overhead. \nTemperatures on the Caprock will cool back down to the upper 90s. \nSadly, triple temperature highs remain forecasted off the Caprock. \nSimilar high temperatures are expected everyday through the weekend \nas the upper pattern doesn't seem to change. The upper ridging will \nremain across southeastern CONUS as the aforementioned upper trough \ndeamplifies. This will allow the upper ridging to retreat back to \nthe west early next week. A passing shortwave on Thursday and \nanother one on Friday will bring chances for some isolated to \nscattered thunderstorms each afternoon and evening, mainly across \nthe far southern Texas Panhandle and portions of the South Plains. \nOtherwise, the rest of the weekend and into early next week look to \nbe dry.",
